{
  "batch": "33-microsoft-deep",
  "title": "macOS Microsoft deeper residuals: Office 365 containers, MAU, Edge, VS Code, PowerShell, Azure Data Studio, Windows App/RDC, OneDrive, Defender, Company Portal/Intune, licensing report-only",
  "path_count": 248,
  "notes": [
    "Deeper Microsoft residual research beyond batch 07-office-electron. Focus: regenerable caches, logs, temps, updater packages, diagnostic zips. Not user documents, Outlook mail profiles, OneDrive CloudStorage sync roots, or license secrets as auto-delete.",
    "Office Group Container UBF8T346G9.Office holds Outlook profiles (mail/attachments). Only FontCache, User Content, SolutionPackages, and explicit log/cache subtrees are delete-eligible; Outlook profile trees are report-only.",
    "OneDrive: never wipe $HOME/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive* or ~/OneDrive* sync roots. Caches/logs/HTTPStorages/updater residuals only.",
    "Office licensing (com.microsoft.office.licensingV2.plist, helper, VL serializer) is report-only. Use Microsoft license removal tool for activation troubleshooting; do not auto-delete.",
    "Defender for Endpoint: diagnostic zips under wdavdiag and install.log are reclaimable; quarantine/ and product install under /Library/Application Support/Microsoft/Defender are report-only (security product).",
    "Power Automate Desktop and Power BI Desktop are Windows-only; no native macOS residual trees. SharePoint sync uses OneDrive client paths.",
    "Close Office, Teams, Edge, OneDrive, VS Code before cleaning container caches."
  ],
  "rules": [
